      "excerpt": "At rank four the selected candidates are $M=v(b_I)$ with\n$4\\in I$, satisfying \\eqref{sv:branch-licence} and exceeding the\ninherited third cap.  Such a change is made only on prefixes that\nalready pass the third cube.  Membership through rank four is\nunchanged and subsequent odd cubes use the new cap.\nThe limiting density difference on a region $\\mathcal C$ is\n\\begin{equation}\\label{sv:even-gain}\n 4\\int_{\\mathcal C}\n \\frac{\\overline F((L-S_r)/t_r)\n                   -\\overline F((M-S_r)/t_r)}\n      {t_1\\cdots t_{r-1}t_r^2}\\,dt_1\\cdots dt_r,\n \\qquad \\overline F=\\frac{F}{2e^\\gamma},\n\\end{equation}\nwhere $r=4$, $L$ is the inherited cap and $M$ the selected endpoint.\nIndeed an even prefix $P_r$ contributes\n$g_N(P_r)V_N^+(N^\\lambda/P_r,p_r)$ to its complete subtree.\nSubtracting the two subtrees gives \\eqref{sv:even-gain}; it is an\nidentity of raw densities before taking an asymptotic limit."
    },
    "ordinary_first_exit_and_parent_rules": {
      "path": "/workspace/chen-imbalanced-semiprimes/paper/release-20261106/en/sieve-appendix.tex",
      "sha256": "15c9f561b870edb43ec1de3a8adf88b0b4561982f0617b58b26b1de966f9f9d8",
      "bytes": 52306,
      "manuscript_commit": "a988cba584d803ae2856a0de50efb582f4f3dd6a",
      "lines": [
        35,
        91
      ],
      "excerpt": "\\end{equation}\nthroughout that region.  The separate three-slot branch with endpoint\n$\\Lambda_{\\rm cap}-3t_3/8$ is subject to the whole-box factorization conditions\nof Appendix~\\ref{app:coefficients}.  A maximum of candidate endpoints\nis always taken over branches satisfying their support conditions.\n\nAn ordinary upper residual tree at total exponent $\\lambda$, after\na prefix of rank $r$, applies the cube tests\n\\begin{equation}\\label{sv:upper-cubes}\n S_{j-1}+3t_j<\\lambda\\qquad(j>r,\\ j\\text{ odd}).\n\\end{equation}\nIf $r$ is even, these are the ordinary upper residual tests.  If $r$\nis odd, they are the ordinary lower residual tests.  The earlier\nmembership decisions are retained.  At an even prefix a change of cap\nis made after admitting the prefix; it introduces no exclusion at that\nrank.  At an odd prefix a cap may be chosen before its own odd test,\nprovided that the decision depends only on that prefix and the\npreviously fixed policy.  Either operation leaves every first\nexclusion at odd full rank.\n\n\\begin{lemma}[First-exit identity]\\label{sv:first-exit}\nLet $\\mathcal T$ be a prefix-closed collection of squarefree products\nfrom a finite prime set $\\mathcal P$, containing the empty product.\nSuppose that all first excluded prefixes have odd rank.  For every\nmultiplicative $\\xi$ with $0\\le \\xi(p)\\le1$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{sv:upper-exit}\n \\sum_{d\\in\\mathcal T}\\mu(d)\\xi(d)\n =\\prod_{p\\in\\mathcal P}(1-\\xi(p))\n +\\sum_{e\\text{ first exit}}\\xi(e)\n           \\prod_{\\substack{p\\in\\mathcal P\\\\p<p_{\\mathrm{last}}(e)}}\n                            (1-\\xi(p)).\n\\end{equation}\nIn particular $\\sum_{d\\mid n,\\ d\\in\\mathcal T}\\mu(d)$ majorizes\n$\\one_{(n,\\prod_{p\\in\\mathcal P}p)=1}$ for every integer $n$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\nEach excluded divisor has a unique first excluded prefix $e$; its\nremaining prime factors are smaller than $p_{\\mathrm{last}}(e)$.\nSumming the complete continuation gives\n$\\mu(e)\\xi(e)\\prod_{p<p_{\\mathrm{last}}(e)}(1-\\xi(p))$.\nSubtract these disjoint continuations from the complete Euler product.\nSince $\\mu(e)=-1$, the sign in \\eqref{sv:upper-exit} is positive.\nTake $\\xi(p)=\\one_{p\\mid n}$ for the last assertion.  The same\nfinite identity applies at $n=0$ and at negative integers.\n\\end{proof}\n\nThe square tests persist through descendants.  A retained odd cube\nimplies its own square.  The following even square follows from\nordering:\n\\begin{equation}\\label{sv:descendant-square}\n S_{j-1}+2t_j\\le S_{j-2}+3t_{j-1}<\\lambda.\n\\end{equation}\nAfter all selected slots have appeared, the expression in\n\\eqref{sv:selected-gate} for any appended slot equals its full square.\nConsequently \\eqref{sv:branch-licence}, checked at the selected prefix,\ncontinues to control the complete descendant vector."
    },
