      "excerpt": "The number $\\Theta$ bounds the complete carrier; $\\Lambda_{\\rm cap}$ bounds the\nhigh-rank levels.  A finite policy specifies a level $N^\\lambda$ at each\nof finitely many prime prefixes.  An ancestor decision is fixed before\nthe children are subdivided.  For decreasing exponents $t_1,\\ldots,t_j$,\nput $S_j=t_1+\\cdots+t_j$.  The full square conditions at an auxiliary\nlevel $N^\\ell$ are\n\\begin{equation}\n S_{j-1}+2t_j\\le\\ell.\n \\label{coef:full-squares}\n\\end{equation}\nIf $I$ is a selected subset of the marked slots, put\n$b_I=\\sum_{i\\in I}t_i$.  In addition to \\eqref{coef:full-squares}, retain\nall the conditions\n\\begin{equation}\n b_I+\\sum_{\\substack{i<j\\\\i\\notin I}}t_i+2t_j\\le\\ell\n \\qquad(j\\notin I).\n \\label{coef:selected-squares}\n\\end{equation}\nFor $j$ after the last selected index, the left side of\n\\eqref{coef:selected-squares} is exactly $S_{j-1}+2t_j$.\nThus adjoining smaller primes preserves the selected conditions whenever\nthe full conditions are preserved.  An admitted cube also implies the\nnext square, since\n\\[\n S_j+2t_{j+1}\\le S_{j-1}+3t_j.\n\\]\nThis observation applies to both parities of the ordinary sieve tree:\nupper first exits have odd rank, and lower first exits have even rank.\n\nThe physical level $\\lambda$ and the auxiliary covering level $\\ell$\nhave different uses.  The coefficient and its density use $\\lambda$;\nfactorization may use a slightly larger $\\ell$.  No change in $\\lambda$\nis made in obtaining this cover.  Here is the needed choice at the\nthree-slot alternative.  Put\n\\[\n A(t)=\\frac{1+t}{2},\\qquad W(z)=\\Lambda_{\\rm cap}-\\frac38z.\n\\]\nOn a coarse box let $\\Gamma=\\inf\\max(A,W)$ and\n$\\lambda=\\Gamma-2e$, where the variation allowance satisfies\n$\\chi<e/10$.  If $\\inf A\\ge\\lambda+e/2$, choose\n$\\ell=\\lambda+e/4$.  Otherwise $\\sup A<\\lambda+11e/20$,\nso $W\\ge\\Gamma$ throughout the box; choose $\\ell=\\lambda+e$.\nThis leaves a reserve of at least $9e/20$ above the lower bound and $e$\nbelow the upper bound.  The remaining initialization reserves include\n\\[\n 1-\\Lambda_{\\rm cap}-2\\mu_0=\\frac3{256},\\qquad\n \\frac{525}{8704}+\\frac{49z}{272}>0.\n\\]\nThe higher-rank changes are restricted to compact pieces on which their\nsupport conditions have positive reserve.  Fine endpoint enlargement is then taken\nsmaller than this reserve."
